From d630bd727d8759006a0e2bdce224fd31c1af73a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dfattal <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:43:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] inline-3d(#83): scroll-shift rects from a measurement-time
 base, not SyncedScrollOffset::Delta

The Phase2 scroll-sync patch (0022) shifts the metadata inline-3d rect lists
by the viewport's impl scroll delta so the weave tracks pixels during a
fling. Its baseline was SyncedScrollOffset::Delta() (active - base), which
assumes the base tracks the commit that supplied the rects. In this browser's
configuration the base never resets after a scroll, so from the first scroll
onward every rect was shifted by the FULL historical offset on every frame,
forever: exclusion rects were driven above the surface and clipped to empty
(page chrome wove - the gallery sticky-header bug family), and when the
tracked channel did not cover a tile its weave rect landed hundreds of px off
(raw SBS / weave applied over empty page). Measured live: delta stuck at
589-1287 device px through 15s of rest.

Fix: Blink stamps the outer-viewport scroll offset (CSS px) AT THE MOMENT the
rects are measured, and it rides the same commit as the rects
(CommitState.inline_3d_scroll_base -> LayerTreeImpl, pushed on commit and
activation). MakeCompositorFrameMetadata then shifts by
(current impl offset - measured-at offset): identically zero at rest, exact
during flings, and self-consistent regardless of commit timing - including
through LayerTreeHost::SetInline3DRects' dedup early-out, since a skipped
commit keeps the old (rects, base) PAIR. The TreesInViz-in-viz client-copy
path carries no base and now gets NO shift (an unshifted one-frame-stale rect
still clears the 70% match gate; a mis-based shift never does).
